# Copy only what you need into backend/.env (never commit real values).
#
# === Meta — "Connect" button (one Facebook *app* for your whole product) ===
# META_APP_ID
#   Numeric App ID: developers.facebook.com → your app → App settings → Basic.
#
# META_APP_SECRET   (same meaning as FACEBOOK_APP_SECRET or FB_APP_SECRET if you use those names)
#   App *Secret* from that same Basic settings page (click "Show"). It is a short
#   fixed string tied to the app — NOT META_FACEBOOK_ACCESS_TOKEN, NOT a Page token,
#   NOT a User long-lived token. Those belong to accounts, not the app shell.
#   One line, no quotes unless your host requires them; no trailing spaces.
#
# If the API returns: Facebook reports "Error validating client secret"
#   → META_APP_SECRET is wrong for this META_APP_ID (typo, old secret after reset,
#   secret from a different Meta app, or a page/user token pasted by mistake).
#   Open App settings → Basic → Show (or Reset) App Secret → paste only that
#   value into META_APP_SECRET → save backend/.env → restart the API → Connect again.
#
# META_REDIRECT_URI
#   Must exactly match a Valid OAuth Redirect URI for this app (e.g. your
#   FlowPilot URL + /auth/meta/callback).
#
# META_GRAPH_API_VERSION=v22.0
#
# === Multi-user ===
# Each workspace user clicks Connect; Meta returns tokens for *their* Pages.
# Those tokens are stored encrypted in the database (social_accounts), not in .env.
# .env only holds *your* developer app id + app secret so OAuth can start.
#
# === LinkedIn (same idea) ===
# LINKEDIN_CLIENT_ID, LINKEDIN_CLIENT_SECRET, LINKEDIN_REDIRECT_URI
# If LINKEDIN_REDIRECT_URI is omitted, backend auto-builds:
#   <FLOWPILOT_PUBLIC_ORIGIN>/linkedin/callback
#
# === OAuth security (server-wide, not per customer) ===
# OAUTH_STATE_SECRET
#   Random string used to sign the OAuth "state" parameter (CSRF protection).
#   One value for the server — not each end-user's secret.
#
# === App origin (for local/prod auto callback URLs) ===
# FLOWPILOT_PUBLIC_ORIGIN
#   Local example: http://localhost:3000
#   Prod example: https://flowpilot.officekithr.net
# If META_REDIRECT_URI is omitted, backend auto-builds:
#   <FLOWPILOT_PUBLIC_ORIGIN>/auth/meta/callback
